{"scraped_at": "2026-06-04T07:26:16.694941+00:00", "run_id": "20260604_072616", "page": 144, "api_response": {"count": 3946, "per_page": 20, "current_page": 144, "total_pages": 198, "next": "https://tripadvisor-scraper-api.omkar.cloud/reviews?query=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.tripadvisor.com%2FAttraction_Review-g293890-d310712-Reviews-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html&page=145&sort_by=most_recent&locale=en-US", "previous": "https://tripadvisor-scraper-api.omkar.cloud/reviews?query=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.tripadvisor.com%2FAttraction_Review-g293890-d310712-Reviews-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html&page=143&sort_by=most_recent&locale=en-US", "results": [{"review_id": 243815390, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r243815390-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "A very holy place", "text": "The temple itself is intricately carved and beautiful. Only hindus are allowed into the temple. Other tourists are only allowed in the temple grounds.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2014-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "64D61303487C60DE56B12A457935DDDB", "name": "sujax", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/sujax", "username": "sujax", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/05/b3/74/5c/sujax.jpg", "contribution_count": 65, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 1007652, "location_name": "Lac-Simon", "location_name_detailed": "Lac-Simon, Canada"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2014-12-10", "published_at_date": "2014-12-10"}, {"review_id": 243776185, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r243776185-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "OM...God Shiva", "text": "Pashupatinath Temple is one of the Hindu Temple in the city of Kathmandu, Nepal...Only Hindus are allowed to visit...\nCannot take the leather things like Belt, Purse, Slippers, Shoes inside the temple...\nThere are lots of beliefs about this temple...\nThe main Pujaris are from South India called Bhatji...\nThere are lot of monkeys also and need to be careful of your belongings...\nBehind the temple is the Bagmati River where the dead people are burned...called burning ghat...\nThe temple is very big...\nI have visited this temple many times...\n", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2014-02-28"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "B6D83AC5B20A06BB78A6783270F36864", "name": "mukeshcn", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/mukeshcn", "username": "mukeshcn", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-s/01/d9/47/ef/mukeshcn.jpg", "contribution_count": 20, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2014-12-09", "published_at_date": "2014-12-09"}, {"review_id": 243602042, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r243602042-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "\"Bit dirty but that will do it...\"", "text": "The place is bit dirty but isn't so much disgusting. Though the feeling of strong divinities being around gives you quite a chill. I saw this place much more maintained than other places in kathmandu. And like every other places in Kathmandu this temple has very ancient history too. ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": null}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "205887A9FF2AC3ECE9ECAC9D4F27D909", "name": "free_traveller22", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/free_traveller22", "username": "free_traveller22", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/df/99/default-avatar-2020-40.jpg", "contribution_count": 9, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2014-12-09", "published_at_date": "2014-12-09"}, {"review_id": 243481791, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r243481791-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Moving insight", "text": "For those not informed in the Hindu way of death and burning of bodies this is very informative and moving. You will be rewarded by getting a guide too. I'm not a guide type of person but I'm glad I did. This is not a cheap day by Kathmandu standards once to travel there pay entrance and get a guide but I feel it's worth the trip.I would suggest not paying the Sadhu the crazy money they ask for pictures and watch out for the monkeys. ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": null, "stay_date": "2014-12-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "73BADF6EF4B550CD619429125AAA6EB2", "name": "Willaim S", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/784willaims", "username": "784willaims", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/16/74/3b/18/willaim-s.jpg", "contribution_count": 93, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 190742, "location_name": "Slough", "location_name_detailed": "Slough, United Kingdom"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2014-12-08", "published_at_date": "2014-12-08"}, {"review_id": 243471438, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r243471438-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Lots of Monkeys :)", "text": "This was an experience I enjoyed.  You were able to see family members saying goodbye to their loved ones who passed away and their rituals they do before cremation.  It is very different from the Westernized world and I would highly recommend going.  Do be careful with the many monkeys that hang around and keep your valuables close. ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 2, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2014-11-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "AC97ED8347A4889C268A6B1EB2BDBDD7", "name": "JBUG1985", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/JBUG1985", "username": "JBUG1985", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/06/dd/74/a9/jbug1985.jpg", "contribution_count": 38, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 60922, "location_name": "Salt Lake City", "location_name_detailed": "Salt Lake City, Utah"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2014-12-08", "published_at_date": "2014-12-08"}, {"review_id": 243279948, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r243279948-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Dirty", "text": "Went there as it is a must do if in Kathmandu. Was very disappointed with how dirty the temple premises were.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 2, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2014-11-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "5BD89D2FFAB7217593B7E928F8B152BA", "name": "PranayMaini", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/PranayMaini", "username": "PranayMaini", "avatar": "https://dynamic-m